WEBVTT

00:00:02.940 --> 00:00:05.020
<b>Fuurin Academy Private Middle School</b>

00:00:02.940 --> 00:00:05.020
<b>Fuurin Academy Private Middle School</b>

00:00:02.940 --> 00:00:05.020
<b>Fuurin Academy Private Middle School</b>

00:00:17.850 --> 00:00:18.740
Here.

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:20.610
Batting's open.

00:00:20.610 --> 00:00:21.700
Who's next?

00:00:22.720 --> 00:00:25.060
Me, me! I'll do some!

00:00:25.060 --> 00:00:26.590
Thank you, Anita.

00:00:26.590 --> 00:00:28.420
Sakura-senpai!

00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:30.390
The bullpen's open now!

00:00:30.390 --> 00:00:32.130
Oh, I'm good for now.

00:00:32.540 --> 00:00:34.330
Why don't you bat, too?

00:00:34.820 --> 00:00:36.840
Huh? Ya ain't gonna pitch?

00:00:38.300 --> 00:00:40.260
Bring it on!

00:02:19.160 --> 00:02:24.080
<b>...With You Again!</b>

00:02:25.770 --> 00:02:26.660
Huh?

00:02:26.660 --> 00:02:28.460
Permission to use the floodlights?

00:02:28.460 --> 00:02:29.620
Y-Yeah.

00:02:29.780 --> 00:02:32.400
Nishina wants to stay later
to practice some more.

00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:37.920
The sun's going down earlier and earlier,
and Anita would probably join him, too.

00:02:38.450 --> 00:02:42.140
Why? I said we could just carry on like before.

00:02:43.770 --> 00:02:47.360
Increasing training time
without a plan won't do the trick.

00:02:47.890 --> 00:02:49.290
You can't just do that.

00:02:49.290 --> 00:02:53.030
Uh, yeah, but it's only for
people who want to stay later.

00:02:53.030 --> 00:02:54.180
Nobody's forcing them—

00:02:54.180 --> 00:02:55.480
I'm against it.

00:02:55.480 --> 00:02:58.820
Everyone else will feel peer-pressured
into staying behind.

00:02:59.170 --> 00:03:02.880
Besides, if we leave someone 
like Nishina to his own devices,

00:03:02.880 --> 00:03:05.070
he might overdo it and injure himself.

00:03:07.130 --> 00:03:10.690
You need to shut that kind of
talk down right away, Mutsuko.

00:03:10.690 --> 00:03:11.420
What's <i>that</i> mean?

00:03:12.070 --> 00:03:13.880
Then <i>you</i> tell them that to their faces.

00:03:14.330 --> 00:03:15.600
I'm not doing it.

00:03:15.600 --> 00:03:18.960
Both Nishina and Anita
genuinely want to aim higher.

00:03:19.250 --> 00:03:22.370
Blocking them from 
practicing more is cruel!

00:03:25.420 --> 00:03:26.470
What is this?

00:03:27.030 --> 00:03:28.600
What do you want?

00:03:32.350 --> 00:03:34.150
I...

00:03:34.150 --> 00:03:36.230
I only had the best of intentions!

00:03:36.790 --> 00:03:41.450
This whole time, I gave 
everything I had... for the team!

00:03:43.470 --> 00:03:47.310
I did... everything I could...

00:03:48.220 --> 00:03:50.650
What should I have done differently?!

00:03:52.670 --> 00:03:53.870
Wai— Daigo!

00:04:00.230 --> 00:04:01.260
Daigo?

00:04:04.190 --> 00:04:05.400
Daigo!

00:04:06.180 --> 00:04:08.430
m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100

00:04:06.180 --> 00:04:08.430
m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100

00:04:06.180 --> 00:04:08.430
<b>Baseball Team</b>

00:04:15.350 --> 00:04:16.810
Nurse's Office

00:04:20.240 --> 00:04:21.400
Sakura-san.

00:04:22.060 --> 00:04:24.050
We've contacted his mother.

00:04:24.050 --> 00:04:26.190
You can go back to class now.

00:04:26.770 --> 00:04:27.700
Yes, ma'am.

00:04:27.700 --> 00:04:29.660
Nurse's Office

00:04:41.510 --> 00:04:43.090
I...

00:04:43.090 --> 00:04:44.680
I only had the best of intentions!

00:04:46.260 --> 00:04:50.970
This whole time, I gave 
everything I had... for the team!

00:04:52.560 --> 00:04:55.040
What should I have done differently?!

00:04:58.690 --> 00:05:00.940
<b>Mifune Public Hospital</b>

00:04:58.690 --> 00:05:00.940
<b>Mifune Public Hospital</b>

00:04:58.690 --> 00:05:00.940
<b>Mifune
Public\h\h</b>

00:04:58.690 --> 00:05:00.940
<b>Hospital</b>

00:04:58.690 --> 00:05:00.940
<b>Mifune\h
Public</b>

00:04:58.690 --> 00:05:00.940
<b>Hospital</b>

00:05:01.880 --> 00:05:03.650
Thank you very much.

00:05:04.130 --> 00:05:06.620
Ma'am, could I have a word with just you?

00:05:06.620 --> 00:05:07.850
Oh, sure.

00:05:07.850 --> 00:05:09.290
Just wait right here.

00:05:09.290 --> 00:05:10.010
Okay.

00:05:11.030 --> 00:05:13.200
<i>And next up, the weather.</i>

00:05:14.840 --> 00:05:19.080
Your son seems to have suffered 
an emotional breakdown.

00:05:19.700 --> 00:05:23.120
He must have been dealing
with a lot of anxiety or stress.

00:05:23.120 --> 00:05:24.710
Stress?

00:05:24.710 --> 00:05:29.660
It'd be best if a family member asks him
what's weighing so heavily on his heart.

00:05:30.970 --> 00:05:33.160
<i>Showers in the afternoon, huh?</i>

00:05:33.800 --> 00:05:36.270
<i>What should I do for our indoor drills?</i>

00:05:39.020 --> 00:05:40.110
What's this?

00:05:40.110 --> 00:05:41.890
You look pretty healthy to me.

00:05:45.820 --> 00:05:48.200
Found ya, Mr. Bunks Off Early.

00:05:48.660 --> 00:05:49.620
Bang!

00:05:53.920 --> 00:05:55.660
What? Mutsuko?

00:05:56.040 --> 00:05:59.630
She went to the hospital to check on Daigo.

00:05:59.630 --> 00:06:01.310
Oh, I see.

00:06:01.310 --> 00:06:03.460
I was a little worried.

00:06:03.950 --> 00:06:08.400
I'm worried for our captain, too, but I was 
wondering if our vice-captain was okay.

00:06:08.400 --> 00:06:11.880
Uh, you don't have to
hide like that, you know.

00:06:11.880 --> 00:06:14.300
It's lunch break, so you look super suspicious.

00:06:14.300 --> 00:06:16.180
Oh. Sorry.

00:06:16.490 --> 00:06:18.930
I know what you mean, though.

00:06:21.730 --> 00:06:24.890
I've noticed for a while now.

00:06:24.890 --> 00:06:27.440
Muttsu hasn't pitched at all
since the Tsujidou game.

00:06:31.380 --> 00:06:34.030
<i>Weighing heavy on his heart, huh?</i>

00:06:34.030 --> 00:06:37.080
<i>He's not the type to talk 
about what's bothering him.</i>

00:06:37.310 --> 00:06:38.360
Kaoru-san?

00:06:39.480 --> 00:06:41.500
Mom? And Dad, too!

00:06:41.850 --> 00:06:43.260
What are you doing here?

00:06:43.260 --> 00:06:46.280
Oh, Goro filled us in on what happened.

00:06:46.280 --> 00:06:48.220
About Dai-chan collapsing.

00:06:48.220 --> 00:06:51.990
Oh, um, I'm sorry we made you worry like that.

00:06:51.990 --> 00:06:55.180
<i>Jeez, that idiot! I told him not
to make a big deal out of it!</i>

00:06:55.560 --> 00:06:56.900
So how is Daigo?

00:06:56.900 --> 00:06:58.390
How is he doing?

00:06:58.810 --> 00:07:01.390
He's calmed down now and is doing fine.

00:07:01.390 --> 00:07:02.740
That's great.

00:07:02.740 --> 00:07:04.650
Where is he?

00:07:04.650 --> 00:07:06.310
Huh? Daigo?

00:07:07.860 --> 00:07:11.070
Pop

00:07:07.860 --> 00:07:11.070
Teeheehee

00:07:07.860 --> 00:07:11.070
I've taken our son

00:07:08.590 --> 00:07:09.700
<i>Teeheehee.</i>

00:07:09.700 --> 00:07:11.050
<i>I've taken our son.</i>

00:07:11.070 --> 00:07:23.420
Finding yourself after 40

00:07:11.070 --> 00:07:23.420
Second career & life

00:07:11.340 --> 00:07:12.570
That's what he said.

00:07:12.570 --> 00:07:14.240
That's Goro for you.

00:07:14.240 --> 00:07:16.730
I wonder if he's trying to cheer him up.

00:07:16.730 --> 00:07:18.390
I wonder...

00:07:18.390 --> 00:07:20.760
Guess ol' Gram and Gramps aren't needed here.

00:07:20.760 --> 00:07:22.150
I'm sorry!

00:07:22.150 --> 00:07:23.130
Excuse me...

00:07:23.740 --> 00:07:25.220
Mutsuko-chan!

00:07:26.890 --> 00:07:29.150
I hope I'm not interrupting.

00:07:29.150 --> 00:07:30.850
Not at all. Right?

00:07:30.850 --> 00:07:31.860
Right.

00:07:31.860 --> 00:07:33.380
Are you a friend of Dai-chan's?

00:07:33.380 --> 00:07:36.360
Yes. I'm the vice-captain of
our team. My name's Sakura.

00:07:36.360 --> 00:07:38.910
I'm Daigo's pop's father.

00:07:39.640 --> 00:07:41.820
His grandfather and grandmother.

00:07:42.940 --> 00:07:44.960
We'll see you later, Kaoru-san.

00:07:44.960 --> 00:07:46.650
Thanks for coming.

00:07:46.960 --> 00:07:47.980
Bye-bye!

00:07:48.870 --> 00:07:51.700
It looks like Daigo was hyperventilating.

00:07:51.700 --> 00:07:54.260
They said an emotional trigger caused it.

00:07:54.260 --> 00:07:55.910
Emotional?

00:07:56.380 --> 00:07:59.330
We were talking about 
the team when he collapsed.

00:07:59.330 --> 00:08:01.890
Maybe I said something I shouldn't have.

00:08:01.890 --> 00:08:04.740
Oh, no, Daigo's problem is with himself.

00:08:04.740 --> 00:08:05.920
Don't blame yourself.

00:08:05.920 --> 00:08:11.420
But he's in this state
because our team is so weak.

00:08:12.450 --> 00:08:17.790
Ever since that huge loss to Tsujidou,
the team's been shaky.

00:08:18.360 --> 00:08:20.350
Oh, and Hikaru-kun was at Tsujidou, too...

00:08:21.580 --> 00:08:23.060
Hikaru-kun?

00:08:23.830 --> 00:08:28.160
♫ I've got a dream only I can see ♫ 

00:08:28.160 --> 00:08:33.090
♫ A man gets lost on the way ♫ 

00:08:33.090 --> 00:08:38.280
♫ Chasing that huge dream ♫ 

00:08:35.860 --> 00:08:39.580
Oh, come on. Stop singing that
random song over and over, will you?

00:08:41.410 --> 00:08:44.680
Anyway, you didn't have to come
all the way home from Kochi

00:08:44.680 --> 00:08:46.500
just because I felt a little sick.

00:08:46.800 --> 00:08:48.000
You bonehead.

00:08:48.000 --> 00:08:52.920
I rushed home 'cause your mother 
told me my sweet son had collapsed!

00:08:53.550 --> 00:08:56.010
Anyway, I'm glad you're all right.

00:08:56.290 --> 00:09:00.000
But hyperventilating... Doesn't that
mean it's an emotional problem?

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:01.100
Something happen?

00:09:03.680 --> 00:09:04.600
Not really.

00:09:05.800 --> 00:09:08.850
Anyway, you don't have to take me home.
Drive me back to school.

00:09:08.850 --> 00:09:10.360
I still have class.

00:09:10.360 --> 00:09:14.320
Restaurant

00:09:10.360 --> 00:09:14.320
Restaurant

00:09:10.630 --> 00:09:11.670
I see.

00:09:11.670 --> 00:09:14.320
I bet you haven't had lunch yet, though.

00:09:14.320 --> 00:09:15.180
Huh?

00:09:14.320 --> 00:09:17.410
Restaurant

00:09:14.320 --> 00:09:17.410
Restaurant

00:09:15.180 --> 00:09:17.050
It's fine. I'm not hungry!

00:09:17.050 --> 00:09:20.140
How are you gonna get
big if you don't eat, dork?

00:09:21.370 --> 00:09:23.030
See, when I was your age,

00:09:23.030 --> 00:09:27.830
they even had these weird high schools where 
the entrance exam was to wolf down five meals.

00:09:28.620 --> 00:09:31.510
Hey, Pop, this isn't the way to my school.

00:09:30.970 --> 00:09:35.800
♫ Oh oh oh huge dream! ♫ 

00:09:33.110 --> 00:09:35.800
Not this song again!

00:09:35.800 --> 00:09:37.260
\hShichikai
Batting Center

00:09:39.850 --> 00:09:41.760
You're opening up way too fast!

00:09:41.760 --> 00:09:43.390
You need to make a wall! A wall!

00:09:43.390 --> 00:09:45.980
<i>Why'd we come to the batting cages?</i>

00:09:47.520 --> 00:09:50.810
Kaoru

00:09:47.520 --> 00:09:50.810
I've reported you,
\hkidnapper!!

00:09:47.520 --> 00:09:50.810
So about Daigo,
the doc thinks it's some
\hkind of psychological issue.

00:09:48.330 --> 00:09:50.810
<i>I've reported you, kidnapper!</i>

00:09:51.650 --> 00:09:55.030
<i>So, about Daigo...</i>

00:10:06.830 --> 00:10:09.540
I said I want to go back to school!

00:10:07.960 --> 00:10:09.540
\hShichikai
Batting Center

00:10:10.260 --> 00:10:12.740
So why are we going to play catch now?

00:10:12.740 --> 00:10:15.600
Oh, come on. After you bat, you catch!

00:10:15.600 --> 00:10:17.620
It's the natural flow of things!

00:10:17.620 --> 00:10:18.930
Or is it the other way around?

00:10:18.930 --> 00:10:20.730
Well, it's fine either way!

00:10:20.730 --> 00:10:24.640
♫ Huge dream... ♫ 

00:10:22.380 --> 00:10:24.640
I said enough with the singing!

00:10:25.520 --> 00:10:26.830
You know what? Fine.

00:10:26.830 --> 00:10:29.320
I'll just run back to school.

00:10:29.320 --> 00:10:30.320
Hey, now.

00:10:30.320 --> 00:10:32.760
How many kilometers is your school from here?

00:10:32.760 --> 00:10:34.140
Class will be over.

00:10:34.140 --> 00:10:35.280
I've got practice today.

00:10:37.280 --> 00:10:41.310
Say what? But I thought
you were done with all that?

00:10:41.310 --> 00:10:44.710
I thought you'd decided to have fun
playing casual baseball with the girls.

00:10:46.880 --> 00:10:50.830
I'm only going by the text I got from
your mom, so I don't know all the details,

00:10:51.420 --> 00:10:53.590
but I hear you got demolished. By Hikaru.

00:10:55.880 --> 00:10:59.530
He's really something, huh? From wheelchair
to comeback trail in just two years.

00:10:59.530 --> 00:11:02.720
And he's a catcher, just like his dad.
And he wears the #3 shirt.

00:11:03.420 --> 00:11:05.180
He must've really pushed himself.

00:11:06.860 --> 00:11:08.940
As if pushing yourself is all it takes.

00:11:09.500 --> 00:11:13.250
Unlike <i>some</i> disappointing son, he's a genius!

00:11:13.780 --> 00:11:17.610
Hey, now. Why can't you just be happy for him?

00:11:17.610 --> 00:11:18.720
He's your friend, right?

00:11:18.720 --> 00:11:21.700
Why begrudge him for making
a comeback after a bad injury?

00:11:21.700 --> 00:11:22.780
I <i>was</i> happy for him!

00:11:23.080 --> 00:11:25.680
But then he started
provoking me and mocking me!

00:11:26.300 --> 00:11:28.830
Saying stuff like I was soft,
 playing house with the girls,

00:11:28.830 --> 00:11:30.790
and that we were in different worlds now.

00:11:31.070 --> 00:11:34.290
Saying he had to stop pitching 
because of that injury!

00:11:36.300 --> 00:11:39.120
Then, they completely wiped the floor with us.

00:11:39.120 --> 00:11:41.260
So how the hell <i>can</i> I be happy for him?!

00:11:47.100 --> 00:11:51.230
The girls are giving everything they've got.
But we're short on players and guidance.

00:11:52.270 --> 00:11:55.190
We can't beat a team of Tsujidou's 
caliber with what we've got.

00:11:56.160 --> 00:11:57.580
So I've accepted it.

00:11:58.050 --> 00:12:02.450
Not all of us can play baseball like you
or Hikaru, with our sights set at the very top.

00:12:03.070 --> 00:12:04.950
If we can't reach the summit of Mount Fuji,

00:12:04.950 --> 00:12:06.950
we've got no hope of climbing Mount Everest!

00:12:14.960 --> 00:12:16.670
<b>Fuurin Academy Private Middle School</b>

00:12:14.960 --> 00:12:16.670
<b>Fuurin Academy Private Middle School</b>

00:12:14.960 --> 00:12:16.670
<b>Fuurin Academy Private Middle School</b>

00:12:18.450 --> 00:12:22.880
Ya can't jus' suppress your feelings of wantin'
to play baseball to yer heart's content.

00:12:23.410 --> 00:12:25.610
It'll wreck yer body.

00:12:25.610 --> 00:12:28.600
That's what made Shigeno-senpai collapse.

00:12:30.040 --> 00:12:33.150
You remember what Tao-senpai said, right?

00:12:33.150 --> 00:12:35.460
She said the magic spell had broken.

00:12:35.460 --> 00:12:37.380
Right, that stuff 'bout Cinderella.

00:12:37.380 --> 00:12:39.550
What's with that "magic" crap, anyways?!

00:12:39.550 --> 00:12:42.970
I ain't ever had no magic helpin' me out.

00:12:42.970 --> 00:12:45.200
It wasn't like Cinderella, but for me,

00:12:45.460 --> 00:12:48.390
I started playing baseball
because I saw Chiyo doing it.

00:12:48.390 --> 00:12:50.330
Then, I started playing with you, Anita,

00:12:50.330 --> 00:12:52.940
and I've only ever had
good times playing baseball.

00:12:52.940 --> 00:12:56.090
That feels like magic to me.

00:12:56.090 --> 00:12:58.790
A spell you and Chiyo cast on me.

00:12:59.120 --> 00:13:01.000
Me? On you?

00:13:01.000 --> 00:13:01.920
Yeah!

00:13:01.920 --> 00:13:04.470
A spell that made me like 
baseball more and more!

00:13:05.500 --> 00:13:06.570
I guess yer right.

00:13:06.570 --> 00:13:10.930
There was that time I almost quit, but ya
cast a magic spell to make me keep going.

00:13:11.130 --> 00:13:12.630
Right?

00:13:12.630 --> 00:13:15.180
And... bam!

00:13:15.850 --> 00:13:17.520
I just cast it again.

00:13:18.980 --> 00:13:20.840
It's workin'! It's workin'!

00:13:20.840 --> 00:13:23.620
I was wondering who was being so loud.

00:13:25.510 --> 00:13:26.910
What are you doing?

00:13:26.910 --> 00:13:28.330
Magic!

00:13:28.330 --> 00:13:29.910
Play baseball!

00:13:29.910 --> 00:13:31.870
I don't need any magic.

00:13:32.280 --> 00:13:36.330
I'm gonna get better and 
get my revenge on Tsujidou!

00:13:37.380 --> 00:13:39.920
The spell totally worked on him.

00:13:39.920 --> 00:13:41.510
It was super effective.

00:13:41.510 --> 00:13:44.290
Cinderella? More like 
Cinder-hella not defeated!

00:13:44.290 --> 00:13:46.050
Was that supposed to be a joke?

00:13:49.530 --> 00:13:51.620
You know, I was thinking...

00:13:51.620 --> 00:13:52.540
Hm?

00:13:52.540 --> 00:13:56.010
About how we just randomly 
started playing baseball.

00:13:56.010 --> 00:13:57.590
Yeah, guess it was random.

00:13:57.590 --> 00:14:01.550
And we didn't really think 
in terms of guys or girls.

00:14:02.430 --> 00:14:05.970
But we always got stared 
at by the other teams.

00:14:05.970 --> 00:14:09.280
Yeah, it was always, "Oh my god, girls!"

00:14:09.280 --> 00:14:11.950
They didn't know anything about us, I guess.

00:14:11.950 --> 00:14:16.120
The guys on our team didn't care, 
'cause they already knew what we were about.

00:14:16.390 --> 00:14:19.210
Those were simpler times.

00:14:20.440 --> 00:14:24.670
I wonder if Daigo really understands 
what we're going through.

00:14:32.050 --> 00:14:35.910
What happens to Cinderella, again?
After the magic wears off, I mean.

00:14:35.910 --> 00:14:36.680
Huh?

00:14:38.840 --> 00:14:41.880
<i>I said I'd run there, but it's 
probably like ten kilometers.</i>

00:14:42.410 --> 00:14:44.650
<i>Should I go back and get him to drive me?</i>

00:14:45.570 --> 00:14:47.410
Oh, hey, Pop!

00:14:47.410 --> 00:14:50.080
Could you... Could you give me a ride?

00:14:50.080 --> 00:14:51.910
This'll take too long.

00:14:52.150 --> 00:14:56.560
My son, if a man declares
something, he sticks to it.

00:14:57.780 --> 00:14:58.870
Wait up.

00:15:00.360 --> 00:15:03.670
Get in. I'll drive you to school.
Just hang out with me first.

00:15:09.910 --> 00:15:11.800
So we're playing catch after all?

00:15:13.950 --> 00:15:15.760
You haven't done anything wrong.

00:15:16.110 --> 00:15:17.010
Huh?

00:15:17.350 --> 00:15:22.030
You did a great job as captain, getting
this far with a team that's got no coach.

00:15:22.030 --> 00:15:25.270
And given you had barely enough players,
your team did great keeping up.

00:15:25.270 --> 00:15:27.020
That's no easy feat.

00:15:28.360 --> 00:15:30.420
So don't hang your head, Daigo.

00:15:30.420 --> 00:15:34.490
It's not your fault, and it's not the 
girls' fault if your team's hit a glass ceiling.

00:15:37.300 --> 00:15:41.400
You saying that won't change anything.

00:15:41.400 --> 00:15:44.170
We can't get to the next level.

00:15:44.170 --> 00:15:46.060
What? So you're just giving up?

00:15:46.060 --> 00:15:47.610
That's no fun.

00:15:47.610 --> 00:15:50.770
It's not a question of "can" or "can't."
It's "Will you do it or won't you?"

00:15:50.770 --> 00:15:52.130
Those are your only choices

00:15:52.630 --> 00:15:54.840
when you really love something.

00:15:56.140 --> 00:15:58.830
That's how Hikaru clawed his way back, right?

00:15:59.820 --> 00:16:00.810
Hikaru...

00:16:01.210 --> 00:16:06.620
He had friends and rivals, and this exciting
dream called baseball he wanted to go back to.

00:16:06.620 --> 00:16:08.520
That's why he pushed himself so hard.

00:16:08.520 --> 00:16:11.680
With nothing but this love 
tightly clenched in his fist.

00:16:12.360 --> 00:16:15.490
A love... for baseball...

00:16:15.490 --> 00:16:20.180
You two feel the same way
about baseball, you and Hikaru.

00:16:20.180 --> 00:16:24.010
You feel it here. Your heart's
telling you it's not enough.

00:16:24.010 --> 00:16:26.460
It's screaming that it wants to play baseball

00:16:26.460 --> 00:16:28.920
more seriously, to the
point that you collapsed!

00:16:35.930 --> 00:16:37.490
It's club time!

00:16:37.490 --> 00:16:40.880
I can't believe you went all the 
way there and just missed him.

00:16:41.410 --> 00:16:45.650
Yeah, but part of me thinks
it's a good thing I didn't see him.

00:16:47.910 --> 00:16:51.020
I wouldn't know what to say to Daigo, anyway.

00:16:51.960 --> 00:16:54.270
He collapsed from the
mental strain he was under.

00:16:54.270 --> 00:16:57.570
I can't just say, "It'll be okay!" or "We'll try harder!"

00:16:58.170 --> 00:16:59.530
Mutsuko...

00:17:04.860 --> 00:17:06.780
I think it's okay to say that.

00:17:07.550 --> 00:17:08.300
Huh?

00:17:09.690 --> 00:17:13.790
I think a team only comes together when you 
let your true feelings smash into each other.

00:17:14.470 --> 00:17:19.680
The captain probably feels the same way.
That's why he let his feelings smash into you.

00:17:20.380 --> 00:17:24.560
Oh, uh, that's just how I read it. I'm sorry.

00:17:24.560 --> 00:17:27.340
No, I think you're right.

00:17:28.250 --> 00:17:34.460
I was so down, I didn't even notice
how much Daigo was suffering.

00:17:35.050 --> 00:17:38.410
Out of everyone on the team,
I was the most blind to it.

00:17:38.410 --> 00:17:39.910
Hey, come on now!

00:17:39.910 --> 00:17:43.960
If <i>you</i> get that down on yourself,
how depressed should <i>I</i> be?!

00:17:43.960 --> 00:17:46.250
And anyway, we're all feeling low,

00:17:46.250 --> 00:17:48.470
and we all hate it!

00:17:48.470 --> 00:17:50.110
Say that to the captain.

00:17:50.110 --> 00:17:52.210
Actually, I want to tell him myself.

00:17:52.440 --> 00:17:54.530
I-I think it's okay to say that.

00:17:55.670 --> 00:17:56.710
All right.

00:17:56.710 --> 00:17:58.130
Let's go say that to Daigo!

00:18:01.560 --> 00:18:02.790
Smash 'em!

00:18:02.790 --> 00:18:06.280
When everybody smashes their feelings 
about baseball into each other,

00:18:06.280 --> 00:18:07.840
that's when you have a team!

00:18:19.860 --> 00:18:21.400
Pop, I'm going.

00:18:25.820 --> 00:18:28.290
<i>That was a good throw, Daigo.</i>

00:18:36.880 --> 00:18:38.590
m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100

00:18:36.880 --> 00:18:38.590
m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100

00:18:36.880 --> 00:18:38.590
<b>Baseball Team</b>

00:18:37.880 --> 00:18:38.590
What?!

00:18:38.810 --> 00:18:40.510
Today's practice is canceled?

00:18:40.510 --> 00:18:41.550
Really?

00:18:41.770 --> 00:18:43.380
I think it's fine.

00:18:43.380 --> 00:18:46.050
Daigo left early. Mutsuko's
gang are off doing something.

00:18:46.050 --> 00:18:47.140
And it's raining.

00:18:47.390 --> 00:18:50.300
Nope, nuh-uh. Sakura-senpai
said she'd jus' be a little late,

00:18:50.300 --> 00:18:52.100
plus we can do our rainy day drills!

00:18:52.100 --> 00:18:54.100
It can be voluntary, then.

00:18:54.100 --> 00:18:55.280
See you later.

00:18:55.280 --> 00:18:56.530
What?!

00:18:56.530 --> 00:18:58.110
Senpai, wait!

00:18:58.740 --> 00:19:01.850
That means ya get even less practice time in!

00:19:01.850 --> 00:19:04.290
You've let yer motivation hit the floor!

00:19:04.290 --> 00:19:05.580
Hey, Anita...

00:19:06.240 --> 00:19:07.570
Don't you get it?

00:19:07.570 --> 00:19:10.040
It's our fault Daigo collapsed.

00:19:11.840 --> 00:19:14.550
We talked about how risky
it was to up our training.

00:19:14.550 --> 00:19:18.560
Before motivation comes into it,
our bodies are the problem.

00:19:18.560 --> 00:19:20.760
That's what was eating at Daigo.

00:19:21.330 --> 00:19:23.720
The gap between the ideal
world and the real world.

00:19:23.720 --> 00:19:27.180
There's no way we can stop Cinderella's clock.

00:19:27.820 --> 00:19:32.150
Magic's one thing, but I don't want to stand
around waiting for some charming prince.

00:19:32.540 --> 00:19:33.540
Later.

00:19:36.520 --> 00:19:37.570
What was that 'bout?

00:19:38.340 --> 00:19:42.620
I'm dumb, so I didn't get a single thing
they were talkin' 'bout.

00:19:43.320 --> 00:19:45.750
Here, Anita, your shoes.

00:19:45.750 --> 00:19:47.060
Thanks.

00:19:48.140 --> 00:19:52.210
So they don't want to wait for a prince?

00:19:52.210 --> 00:19:53.100
Hey!

00:19:53.100 --> 00:19:55.400
The seniors just went home!

00:19:55.400 --> 00:19:56.820
What's going on?

00:19:56.820 --> 00:19:59.010
I got it!

00:19:59.010 --> 00:20:00.970
So here it is. Whisper, whisper, whisper.

00:20:01.590 --> 00:20:02.600
Yer right!

00:20:02.600 --> 00:20:03.930
'Kay, let's go!

00:20:05.170 --> 00:20:06.640
<i>It's really starting to come down.</i>

00:20:09.610 --> 00:20:14.810
Today, we have a very special guest coach.
Shigeno Izumi used to be a Dolphins player.

00:20:15.500 --> 00:20:18.560
But in this rain, we won't be able to train.

00:20:19.780 --> 00:20:21.130
Sorry, everyone!

00:20:21.130 --> 00:20:24.820
So which one of you brought this
rain with them? Or maybe it was me?

00:20:26.010 --> 00:20:27.070
Oh, it's Daigo.

00:20:27.850 --> 00:20:29.520
So it is.

00:20:29.520 --> 00:20:31.270
What's he doing?

00:20:31.270 --> 00:20:32.930
Daigo!

00:20:32.930 --> 00:20:34.670
He can't hear you.

00:20:35.050 --> 00:20:35.990
That's fine.

00:20:36.480 --> 00:20:38.130
<i>Keep going, Daigo.</i>

00:20:38.450 --> 00:20:41.360
All right! Let's ignore the 
rain and practice anyway!

00:20:47.260 --> 00:20:48.970
Shigeno

00:20:47.260 --> 00:20:48.970
Shigeno

00:22:08.570 --> 00:22:09.760
Daigo!

00:22:30.370 --> 00:22:31.470
You guys...

00:22:37.990 --> 00:22:42.300
Hey, Daigo, if you're gonna collapse
'cause you're worrying about us,

00:22:42.300 --> 00:22:44.470
stop holding back and
unleash what you've got!

00:22:45.550 --> 00:22:50.560
After Cinderella's magic spell faded,
she was no longer scared of anything!

00:22:50.560 --> 00:22:52.640
You got that, Daigo?

00:22:52.640 --> 00:22:55.100
I'm definitely no Cinderella.

00:22:55.100 --> 00:22:58.080
I suffer, I get hurt,
I get scared, I get embarrassed.

00:22:58.080 --> 00:23:02.110
But because it's fun,
I love being here with you all!

00:23:02.320 --> 00:23:04.160
Collapsin' is fine!

00:23:04.160 --> 00:23:07.860
Collapse with everythin' ya got, 
then get up with everythin' ya got!

00:23:07.860 --> 00:23:09.950
Jus' get up as many times as you need!

00:23:10.200 --> 00:23:14.030
My dream is to become a wizard.

00:23:14.540 --> 00:23:15.790
A baseball wizard!

00:23:16.070 --> 00:23:19.240
I seriously don't know
what the hell is going on,

00:23:19.240 --> 00:23:21.140
but if we're gonna get covered in mud,

00:23:21.140 --> 00:23:22.750
let's do it in our uniforms!

00:23:23.000 --> 00:23:27.390
Um, well, if Fuurin Middle ever gets a team bus,

00:23:27.780 --> 00:23:29.720
I want it to be a pumpkin carriage!

00:23:29.980 --> 00:23:31.980
Chiyo, that was weird.

00:23:32.480 --> 00:23:34.180
Are we stuck with Cinderella forever?

00:23:36.950 --> 00:23:40.050
Daigo, everyone's already said their piece.

00:23:40.050 --> 00:23:42.600
I don't have anything special 
to add, so I'll just say...

00:23:43.170 --> 00:23:46.640
I hope we can all keep 
playing baseball together!

00:23:52.680 --> 00:23:53.730
Yeah!

00:23:55.000 --> 00:23:56.740
Fuurin!

00:23:57.880 --> 00:24:00.000
Yeah!

00:24:09.280 --> 00:24:12.510
<i>Let's play ball once more!</i>

